{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "First Day of Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Finally, My Workplace "}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 6}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Analyze issues relating to different topics and their solution k written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to devote "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give all or a large part of one's time or resources to a person, activity, or cause"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You'll need to devote some time to establishing general organization techniques that work for you, such as how to arrange your files and who to contact for specific information. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are the words to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "co-worker"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "colleague; a person you work with"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did Ms. Moore mention you would be sharing space with a few co-workers?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "flexibility"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the state of being flexible; able to easily make changes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should include some flexibility in your system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "detail-oriented"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "attentive to small details"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It really helps to be detail-oriented."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "project management "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "organizing the work of different people contributing to a large project"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As editorial assistants, planning is particularly important, especially in relation to project management. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le06ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le06ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Causative <span class=\"italic\">Get</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Have</span> in the Active Pattern"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use causative <span class=\"italic\">get</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have</span> in active and passive voices. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use causative <span class=\"italic\">get</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have</span> in the <span class=\"underline\">active voice</span>, it has the meaning of \u201ccause or order someone to do something\u201d.<br/><br/>  The structure looks like this:<br/><br/>  get + person + infinitive (to + verb)<br/> have + person + verb (infinitive without to)<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I'll <span class=\"strong\">get the waiter to bring</span> the bill.<br/> I'll <span class=\"strong\">have the waiter bring</span> the bill.</span><br/><br/>  There is a slight difference in meaning between <span class=\"italic\">get</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have</span> in this structure. When you <span class=\"italic\">get</span> someone to do something for you, it implies that you need to convince them in some way. <span class=\"italic\">Have</span> is a little more neutral in meaning.<br/><br/>  When you use the causative <span class=\"italic\">get </span>and <span class=\"italic\">have</span> in a <span class=\"underline\">passive voice</span>, it has the meaning of \u201carrange for someone else to do something\u201d. You use this structure when you want to express that you pay or ask someone to do something for you. <br/><br/>  The structures are:<br/><br/>  get + object + past participle<br/> have + object + past participle<br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I have to <span class=\"strong\">get my jacket cleaned</span>.<br/> I'll <span class=\"strong\">have those reports completed</span> for you. </span><br/><br/>  When you use the passive, you come across less direct and therefore more polite."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll have your co-workers introduced to you tomorrow."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Projects get divided into many different tasks. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sometimes, each task has got to be completed before the next one can begin."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Modals to Express Necessity, Duty and Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to express your opinion about what is right and what is wrong, you use the modals <span class=\"italic\">should</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span>. <br/> You use the modals <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">need</span> and their negatives <span class=\"italic\">mustn't</span> and <span class=\"italic\">needn't</span> to talk about what is necessary and not necessary."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In a workplace setting, there are opportunities to discuss duties and to give advice to others.<br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">should</span> take this job seriously. </span>(= it's your duty)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Drivers <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span> be more considerate on the road. </span>(=it's their duty)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">You really <span class=\"strong\">shouldn't</span> be handing in reports late.</span> (= strong advice criticism)<br/><br/>   You need to make sure that the context of the comment is right, otherwise you come across as condescending and rude. <br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"underline\">must and mustn't</span> when you decide for yourself what is necessary. <br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">mustn't</span> keep asking for my help all the time.</span> (= I don't want you to)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">really</span> must be going. </span>(I think I must)<br/><br/>  You can also use <span class=\"italic\">must</span> and <span class=\"italic\">mustn't</span> for impersonal necessity (something that is imposed upon you).<br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">The screw <span class=\"strong\">must</span> be tight for it to hold.</span><br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"underline\">need and needn't</span> to talk about obligations.<br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">need</span> to inform us about any emergencies that prevent you from being at work.<br/>  You <span class=\"strong\">needn't</span> come to dinner if you don't want to.</span> (In this example, the authority comes from the speaker)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You mustn't be concerned by that. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You'll need to devote some time to establishing general organization techniques that work for you, such as how to arrange your files and who to contact for specific information."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Next, you will need to adopt planning strategies. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You must plan your tasks ahead of time to bring the project to fruition. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You mustn't lose track of any part of the project."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ask 5 friends or classmates to describe a problem of organization they may have at work. For example, do they arrive late? Do they lose things? Do they forget meetings?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think about what advice could help each person with each problem."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Go online to find ideas to help people be organized."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose one person to help. Write a letter of 100 - 150 words to that person giving suggestions about how improve their organizational skills. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Proofread your letter. Make sure you use correct spelling and punctuation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your letter aloud."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk to people about about organization at work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read suggestions for improving organization at work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a letter giving advice."}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about my work responsibilities."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express necessity, duty, and advice.  "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can ask someone to do something.  "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you think being organized at work is very important? Why or why not?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What happens if a person is not well organized?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Can you be too organized? How?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": " Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": " Let's review!"}], "template_override": 1}, {